The meeting is over, and I sit at my desk.
My boss comes over to me.
His name is Thomas and he is our project manager.
He smiles broadly and looks very happy.
"Hello, Maya, and welcome to the project," he says.
"We have looked forward to having you with us."
I thank him for the nice words.
He tells a little about our new tasks.
"The whole team has worked hard," he explains.
"We have finally made a complete plan."
He gives me a large folder with documents.
He explains his ideas calmly and clearly.
"As a software engineer, your role is very important," Thomas says.
"Do you have any questions?" he asks.
I look at the documents and shake my head.
"Not yet," I answer with a smile.
"But I will probably ask you later," I add.
"My door is always open," he says and laughs.
He goes back to his office.
I feel truly welcome on the team.
